    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "contrib: require trusted signers in verify.py",
    "user": {
      "login": "enessubass",
      "id": 19182329,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTgyMzI5",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19182329?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/enessubass",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/enessubass/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`verify_shasums_signature` previously separated signatures into `good_trusted` and `good_untrusted`, but computed `num_trusted = len(good_trusted) + len(good_untrusted)`. As a result, 3 valid signatures from untrusted keys present in the local GPG keyring satisfied `--min-good-sigs` even when none of them were trusted in GPG or matched `--trusted-keys`.\n\nIn addition, `README.md` documents passing full 40-character primary key fingerprints to `--trusted-keys`, whereas `parse_gpg_result` only recorded the key identifier from `GOODSIG` and ignored `VALIDSIG` fingerprints, did not deduplicate multiple signatures from the same primary key, and still counted `REVKEYSIG` entries toward the threshold.\n\nChanges:\n- Count only distinct, non-revoked trusted signers toward `--min-good-sigs`.\n- Parse signing and primary key fingerprints from GnuPG `VALIDSIG` status lines so `--trusted-keys` matches full fingerprints while deduplicating by primary key fingerprint.\n- Clarify the trust requirement in `contrib/verify-binaries/README.md`.\n- Add unit tests in `contrib/verify-binaries/test.py` (`python3 -m unittest contrib/verify-binaries/test.py -v`).",
